PURPOSE of /kernel/mce-test/hwpoison
Description: HWPoison test (MCA recovery)
Author: Evan McNabb <emcnabb@redhat.com>

HWPoison description: (from RHEL6 feature page) 
---
The HWPoison feature gives the possibility of recovery from an uncorrectable
memory error incurred by a user process. In the past this would have resulted
in an automatic kernel panic.  When an uncorrectable memory error is detected
the associated memory page is flagged, and all user processes that have mapped
that page are dealt with. For a clean page that has a duplicate backing copy on
disk, the page is invalidated and isolated from future use. The user process
carries on without issue. For a dirty page, the page is unmapped, and should
the user process reference the page again it will be killed.
---

This RHTS test uses mce-test's HWPoison test to software inject errors and
confirm OS correctly kills associated userspace process.
